{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld","id":1433982,"title":"Recoving things lost to the Wyld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-30T21:18:13-08:00","id":1433982,"title":"Recoving things lost to the Wyld","content":"Just had an idea, and wondering if it's setting-beaking or just bad. See, I was thinking how many things have been lost to the Wyld, especially during the Contagion Invasion. I thought what if such things could be recovered. Now, this should not be something for lower level characters, but I did think it should be possible. So, what I'm thinking is: stuff of Creation that has been lost and disolved into the Wyld can be recovered. But, only by some epic quest or very high Essence charms or sorceries. Lunars maybe can use high Essence charm to travel the Wyld to seek out what they want to recover (see, it has to be a specific thing they're searching for).Or, the Solars maybe could develop a charm from the WST tree that could call back or summon something from the Wyld.<br /> <br /> I can't elaborate further yet, this is a brainstorm idea while I'm about 3 Rum&amp;Cokes into my night. But how bad is it so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T21:49:38-08:00","id":1433983,"title":"","content":"Personally, I wouldn't allow a straight-up recovery of territory, people, etc. lost to the Wyld. I think it goes against the general &quot;consequences stay happened&quot; principle of Exalted. If the Exalted or other powers in the setting can't bring a single soul back to life after they've been killed, they <i>certainly</i> shouldn't be able to do it on a mass scale.<br /> <br /> That said, there are probably ways to fake this, effectively. For instance, I'd allow a sorcerous working of some level (probably Solar 2 or 3) to scan the past in sufficient detail that a Solar with Wyld-Shaping Technique could then use that information to essentially recreate a chunk of land, with the inhabitants of it. They wouldn't be the same people, in the sense that there wouldn't be continuity of existence there. But you could do it with sufficiently good reproduction that the inhabitants <i>thought</i> they were the destroyed people.<br /> <br /> Of course, there'd be complications and consequences, because there always are. Fate and destiny might get weird around some of them, for example, as the processes of Creation tried to handle these new individuals popping up who have all the identifying stuff of people they long ago wrote off as dead. And if any of the destroyed people's souls survived, and hadn't reincarnated, they might go &quot;hey, that's the body I'm assigned to! Better pop back in there!&quot;, and get into fights with the Wyld-Shaping Technique-created souls.<br /> <br /> Sounds like an interesting thing to use as the centerpiece of a campaign, if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T00:15:59-08:00","id":1433991,"title":"","content":"so if I wanted to recover SOULS but not the persons attached to them what would that entail?<br /> <br /> I Will bring the Dragon Kings and other dead races back and You WILL NOT stop me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 01-31-2021, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T00:18:48-08:00","id":1433992,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d also say it depends on what you define as \u201cLost to the Wyld.\u201d Were the objects or people or lands stolen by Raksha, stuffed in a big sack, and carried away? Depending on how long it\u2019s been, it could well be recoverable. Were they eroded over time by the tides of chaos, until the things they are no longer resemble the things they were? That\u2019s gonna take some more serious effort. Were they literally dissolved in the rush of unreality as the Crusade hit? I\u2019d suggest at that point that it could only be remade, not \u201crecovered.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T00:33:03-08:00","id":1433993,"title":"","content":"Hey, back ater some thought...I do agree, whatever form this takes...it should be a massive gitchy fuck-job to the Loom....and so there will be consequences...and Sidereal protocols in place to stop the ambitious from doing this in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T01:31:15-08:00","id":1433996,"title":"","content":"IMO the only things that have survived more or less unscathed in the wyld are things in or around manses that managed to stay operational, due to having wyld-stabilizing features in their construction, leaving behind small islands of stability<br /> <br /> My players are currently wracking their minds of how to recover one such manse, which they found in the Deep Wyld, because they need to dismantle it and get the parts to creation for something more useful - problem is... they're afraid that dismantling the manse will mean that the parts themselves will start to boil away into wyld energy, because Deep Wyld (and they're not entirely wrong)<br /> <br /> as for recovering lands or people lost in the wyld during the great contagion or the balloran crusade? I would seek out the courts of the fair folk, find out who took what lands, and perhaps try to draw the memories of the places out of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T02:13:00-08:00","id":1433997,"title":"","content":"damn.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I try","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T04:03:28-08:00","id":1434006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld#post1433982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just had an idea, and wondering if it's setting-beaking or just bad. See, I was thinking how many things have been lost to the Wyld, especially during the Contagion Invasion. I thought what if such things could be recovered. Now, this should not be something for lower level characters, but I did think it should be possible. So, what I'm thinking is: stuff of Creation that has been lost and disolved into the Wyld can be recovered. But, only by some epic quest or very high Essence charms or sorceries. Lunars maybe can use high Essence charm to travel the Wyld to seek out what they want to recover (see, it has to be a specific thing they're searching for).Or, the Solars maybe could develop a charm from the WST tree that could call back or summon something from the Wyld.<br /> <br /> I can't elaborate further yet, this is a brainstorm idea while I'm about 3 Rum&amp;Cokes into my night. But how bad is it so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it.<br /> <br /> The Wyld is &quot;wibbly-wobbly, time-y-why-me&quot; enough to make recovering things lost to the Wyld distinct from conventional time travel and ressurection. Like how 2E allowed time travel within Malfeas.<br /> <br /> I could see passing through a series of trials to make an Unshaped reguritate that which it swallowed. Which might not return things in precisely the same condition as they were lost. Or, worse, perhaps it does return them in <i>exactly </i>the same condition as when they were lost.<br /> <br /> Or an epic quest to chart the form of the roiling madness of the Wyld, and in so charting the Wyld is given form... perhaps a form that would be familiar to those who knew the old shape of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T21:09:26-08:00","id":1434079,"title":"","content":"Reminds of reading about Caerjon. A twin or clone Creation which has made by a Primodial they different want to play with his brothers and sisters. <br /> <br /> The world ended by being burned but UCS whom set the world eternally aflame, since it was lost to the wyld. Stuff like a think could be interesting for high Exalts to find in the Wyld. But finding random low dot artifacts I would be against. The wyld is not a mere slotmachine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T21:30:46-08:00","id":1434082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1433991#post1433991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so if I wanted to recover SOULS but not the persons attached to them what would that entail?<br /> <br /> I Will bring the Dragon Kings and other dead races back and You WILL NOT stop me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall wasnt the big trick with dragon kings getting them to live long enough to start regaining past life awareness and doing their enlightenment thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T21:40:12-08:00","id":1434084,"title":"","content":"*raises hand*<br /> <br /> Here's the question. When you say 'can be recovered' what do you mean? Lore charms, Investigation charms, excellencies and the like mean that you can take entire scraps of information from rumours and recreate entire cultures from it. You can use sorcery to look into the past. If you recreate the lands to be entirely, perfectly the same from before, such that if a Lunar were to walk back into his old homeland and he would struggle to see the difference... is it 'recovered'? If you were to recreate a human being so utterly that only high powered celestial charms can figure out that he's not the same person as the one who died, did you 'resurrect' him? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T00:48:10-08:00","id":1434093,"title":"","content":"How could you ever verify that the thing you're pulling out of the Wyld is really the thing that was lost to it, and not just a new thing born of the creative power of the Wyld and your expectations or preconceptions based on researching what was lost?<br /> <br /> (Also, is there a practical difference, given lack of certainty?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T01:03:54-08:00","id":1434094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434093#post1434093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, is there a practical difference, given lack of certainty?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Both have potential for awesome horror stories where you question the nature of reality, but only one of those options has the treasure you recovered mutating into a freakish extra-dimensional haunt as you obess over whether it is really &quot;real&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T01:04:15-08:00","id":1434095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434093#post1434093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could you ever verify that the thing you're pulling out of the Wyld is really the thing that was lost to it, and not just a new thing born of the creative power of the Wyld and your expectations or preconceptions based on researching what was lost?<br /> <br /> (Also, is there a practical difference, given lack of certainty?)</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Ninja'd<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Very much this.<br /> <br /> But then isn't this the starting point of a lot of good stories? Sure, you've miraculously retrieved your loved ones from the Wyld, but don't they seem OFF to you some how...?<br /> <br /> And why are all your fellow villagers now disappearing...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 02-01-2021, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T01:12:05-08:00","id":1434096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434095#post1434095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Ninja'd<br /> <br /> Very much this.<br /> <br /> But then isn't this the starting point of a lot of good stories? Sure, you've miraculously retrieved your loved ones from the Wyld, but don't they seem OFF to you some how...?<br /> <br /> And why are all your fellow villagers now disappearing...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bonus points if you pull a <i>Transcendence</i> and they are really your loved ones, just kinda traumatised, and have nothing to do with the missing villagers. But you only find out when it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T06:13:52-08:00","id":1434112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434093#post1434093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, is there a practical difference, given lack of certainty?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's a person, then no practical difference between the way the person truly acted, with all their nuances and capacity to defy expectation, and a facsimile formed only from your expectations?<br /> <br /> Only for narcissists and sociopaths, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-01-2021, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T06:26:18-08:00","id":1434113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434093#post1434093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could you ever verify that the thing you're pulling out of the Wyld is really the thing that was lost to it, and not just a new thing born of the creative power of the Wyld and your expectations or preconceptions based on researching what was lost?<br /> <br /> (Also, is there a practical difference, given lack of certainty?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Some barely-functioning First Age enchantment somewhere might care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T08:46:47-08:00","id":1434136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434112#post1434112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's a person, then no practical difference between the way the person truly acted, with all their nuances and capacity to defy expectation, and a facsimile formed only from your expectations?<br /> <br /> Only for narcissists and sociopaths, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's to say the Wyld can't take a set of preconceptions, run them through its creative process, and spit out a person who is for all intents and purposes real?<br /> <br /> You can't tell from the outside if a p-zombie is a p-zombie. That's the point of the idea of p-zombies.<br /> <br /> (The p-zombie thing is just an analogy; I'm pretty sure even Wyld simulacra have internality.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 02-01-2021, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T10:12:52-08:00","id":1434151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434112#post1434112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's a person, then no practical difference between the way the person truly acted, with all their nuances and capacity to defy expectation, and a facsimile formed only from your expectations?<br /> <br /> Only for narcissists and sociopaths, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you expect a person to defy expectations, how can you really tell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T10:55:47-08:00","id":1434154,"title":"","content":"Also, who wouldn't be a bit off after being rescued from the Wyld? Trauma exists.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point I'm making here is split off from a point Jenna made many, many years ago, during discussion surrounding the release of the original <i>Exalted: The Fair Folk</i>. If you take a source of true randomness, then you can get any signal you want out of it provided you apply the right filter. But does that mean the signal came from the randomness, or the filter?<br /> <br /> (&quot;Yes.&quot;)<br /> <br /> The Wyld is a font of infinite creative potential, and the bit about noise, signal, and filter is <i>what infinite creative potential means</i>. Things like Wyld Shaping and Wyld Cauldron and questing against the Wyld turn that potential to the will of the shaper, pulling specific things out of it that exist to various degrees of realness until they interact with Creation sufficiently that their realness becomes lasting. Observing things in the Wyld heightens their temporary realness, and it's never clear <i>to the observer</i> whether the increased detail and reality legible in what they're observing is a function of their noticing more detail, or creating/projecting more detail via their observation.<br /> <br /> So if you rescue someone or something &quot;lost to the Wyld,&quot; do they / does it come from the noise or the filter? Is it the original person or thing, or is it someone or something new created out of your observation, desire, and preconceptions? If you use your Exalted super-Investigation to develop an <i>exceptionally clear idea</i> of what was lost, such that you feel confident you could discern the real thing from a Wyld simulacrum, doesn't that just mean you'll be <i>even better</i> at creating a more accurate Wyld simulacrum? Is &quot;Wyld simulacrum&quot; even a coherent concept at this point?<br /> <br /> If whatever you pull out of the Wyld is a bit off, does that mean they're fake, or are they just exhibiting the natural effects of having had experiences in the Wyld? If you're looking for a fantastic, legendary magical vase sculpted by a famous First Age sculptor that was lost in such-and-such Wyld incursion, and what you get out of the Wyld is a bit warped, is that because you made it wrong or was it warped by spending centuries in the Wyld? If you're too committed to finding the one that <i>isn't</i> warped, are you likely to reject the &quot;real thing&quot; and settle for something you create out of your conceptions instead? Or is refusing to settle for a warped copy and commitment to finding the original... an act of will on your part that can repair the vase to its original state, assuming that being lost to the Wyld means it becomes of the Wyld and becomes subject to the process of Wyld shaping?<br /> <br /> If you pull a <i>person</i> out of the Wyld and they're a bit off, are they a simulacrum or are they exhibiting trauma? If you pull a person out of the Wyld and they act normal for a while but then hulk out and go all The Thing on you, does that mean you pulled a monster out of the Wyld instead or were they the original, warped by the Wyld into a monster?<br /> <br /> You <i>can't</i> know the answers to these questions, unless you, like, declare them out of character as one of the people running the game. But isn't even that kind of analogous to what I'm talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 02-01-2021, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T10:59:19-08:00","id":1434155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434094#post1434094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both have potential for awesome horror stories where you question the nature of reality, but only one of those options has the treasure you recovered mutating into a freakish extra-dimensional haunt as you obess over whether it is really &quot;real&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the potential was having your REAL long-lost lover finally make their way back to you, only to find you in bed with a convincingly-accurate clone of themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T11:02:35-08:00","id":1434157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434136#post1434136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's to say the Wyld can't take a set of preconceptions, run them through its creative process, and spit out a person who is for all intents and purposes real?</div> </div> </div> </div>What even is the Wyld, man.<br /> <br /> If it has a &quot;creative process&quot;, unlike a force of nature, wouldn't it be a living creature of Primordial scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T11:04:10-08:00","id":1434158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434157#post1434157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What even is the Wyld, man.<br /> <br /> If it has a &quot;creative process&quot;, unlike a force of nature, wouldn't it be a living creature of Primordial scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>See my longer post.<br /> <br /> Also, observation-capable entities do seem to self-generate or generate each other within the Wyld, so it's not so much a living creature in that sense as a whole ecosystem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T11:05:31-08:00","id":1434159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434155#post1434155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the potential was having your REAL long-lost lover finally make their way back to you, only to find you in bed with a convincingly-accurate clone of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a problem, but the problem underneath that problem is &quot;Is there even a difference?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T11:31:33-08:00","id":1434163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434155#post1434155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the potential was having your REAL long-lost lover finally make their way back to you, only to find you in bed with a convincingly-accurate clone of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you take me as your wife, foresaking all other wives?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T18:12:40-08:00","id":1434209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434112#post1434112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's a person, then no practical difference between the way the person truly acted, with all their nuances and capacity to defy expectation, and a facsimile formed only from your expectations?<br /> <br /> Only for narcissists and sociopaths, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hell does that mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T19:09:01-08:00","id":1434211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434136#post1434136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's to say the Wyld can't take a set of preconceptions, run them through its creative process, and spit out a person who is for all intents and purposes real?<br /> <br /> You can't tell from the outside if a p-zombie is a p-zombie. That's the point of the idea of p-zombies.<br /> <br /> (The p-zombie thing is just an analogy; I'm pretty sure even Wyld simulacra have internality.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a more complex way I can engage with these and further points (including some of my meaning I believe you've misconstrued), but right now my priority is on how this is a game, and in particular is <i>this</i> game.<br /> <br /> I find this attitude to be very contrary to the usual standards of Exalted regarding player and character agency. A narrative that ends on &quot;you'll never know if this is really who or what you intended to pull out&quot; does not seem well suited.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know, there's the Occult Ability and Charm enhanced insight into people's personalities, I think there are reasonable tools to figure this stuff out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434209#post1434209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hell does that mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>That other people are always more complicated than we can fully consciously recognise, and if one is close enough to them and paying attention then a notable absence of some traits or actions will at least be apparent, even if the cause can't be determined.<br /> <br /> I'm not even saying you'd definitely know they were a conjuration of the Wyld, just the idea of it having a form of &quot;you could never really know&quot; has shortcomings to me.<br /> <br /> Topics similar to this have come up before, and honestly I dislike this line of reasoning on principle because a feel it denotes a very utilitarian approach to human relationships. An idea of Exalted who don't really fully care for or appreciate the person they want to save or restore in their own right, just what function they perform in the life of the Exalt. A substitute can be accepted, because what matters are your feelings.<br /> <br /> And I like to generally promote a perspective on people as complex enough that genuinely creating a true and total simulacrum of them will not work and can be noticeable over time. That there are all kinds of important things, even emergent from small traits, that enhance the inherent worthiness of the individual.<br /> <br /> The thought experiment of &quot;what if you could make a true and indistinguishable replicant of a person&quot; holds no interest to me, as it is too abstracted from meaningful reality. The use as a device in fiction holds no interest to me because I find that abstraction to lack resonance, and I otherwise find it to be a lazy way of generating horror or ambiguity or profundity: raising a question with no genuine significance. I think a roleplaying game adds to that a layer of &quot;I want to jerk the player around in a manner that I think is very clever, provide a solution that may or may not be hollow and disregard means of tapping the surface and listening&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T19:11:23-08:00","id":1434212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434157#post1434157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What even is the Wyld, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>A whimsical font of surprises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T02:15:34-08:00","id":1434238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434211#post1434211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a more complex way I can engage with these and further points (including some of my meaning I believe you've misconstrued), but right now my priority is on how this is a game, and in particular is <i>this</i> game.<br /> <br /> I find this attitude to be very contrary to the usual standards of Exalted regarding player and character agency. A narrative that ends on &amp;quot;you'll never know if this is really who or what you intended to pull out&amp;quot; does not seem well suited.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know, there's the Occult Ability and Charm enhanced insight into people's personalities, I think there are reasonable tools to figure this stuff out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the Exalted could develop Charms to work out the nature of a person who has come from the Wyld. Just like Jonathan Strange was able to dig up the fae lump of driftwood he thought was his wife. If a character wants to go on a journey of exploration, I'm happy to take them on that journey.<br /> <br /> Because there's a story of discovery to be told there.<br /> <br /> The Exalted can fight the Primordials. But that doesn't mean that you spend 8XP and the Primordials immediately yield to you.<br /> <br /> This is a story of loss -- and the recovery from the Wyld is a part of that loss -- which evolves into a story of introspective horror, of personal discovery matched with an exploration of human dynamics and the world around you.<br /> <br /> Which is fine if it doesn't appeal to you. I'll not make you play out the story of Orpheus recovering his wife any more than I'll make you play out Zeus battling Chronus. But both stories <i>are</i> fertile for playing out in a game (heck, that's basically the entire premise of Changeling the Lost), and in <i>this</i> game (about world shaping mystic heroes and their too human foibles).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That other people are always more complicated than we can fully consciously recognise, and if one is close enough to them and paying attention then a notable absence of some traits or actions will at least be apparent, even if the cause can't be determined.<br /> <br /> I'm not even saying you'd definitely know they were a conjuration of the Wyld, just the idea of it having a form of &amp;quot;you could never really know&amp;quot; has shortcomings to me.<br /> <br /> Topics similar to this have come up before, and honestly I dislike this line of reasoning on principle because a feel it denotes a very utilitarian approach to human relationships. An idea of Exalted who don't really fully care for or appreciate the person they want to save or restore in their own right, just what function they perform in the life of the Exalt. A substitute can be accepted, because what matters are your feelings.<br /> <br /> And I like to generally promote a perspective on people as complex enough that genuinely creating a true and total simulacrum of them will not work and can be noticeable over time. That there are all kinds of important things, even emergent from small traits, that enhance the inherent worthiness of the individual.<br /> <br /> The thought experiment of &amp;quot;what if you could make a true and indistinguishable replicant of a person&amp;quot; holds no interest to me, as it is too abstracted from meaningful reality. The use as a device in fiction holds no interest to me because I find that abstraction to lack resonance, and I otherwise find it to be a lazy way of generating horror or ambiguity or profundity: raising a question with no genuine significance. I think a roleplaying game adds to that a layer of &amp;quot;I want to jerk the player around in a manner that I think is very clever, provide a solution that may or may not be hollow and disregard means of tapping the surface and listening&amp;quot;. </div> </div> </div>I'm having trouble parsing this line of thought:<br /> <br /> People are more than what we notice about them.<br /> So they'll lack important traits.<br /> And we'll notice those missing traits.<br /> Which we can't notice.<br /> <br /> I take your wider point. It rings very Stepford Wives -- the traits we value, or think we value, are often incidental to the traits that make the person. And this kind of utilitarian approach can devalue meaningful relationships. No contest your honor, a person is more than what they are <i>too me</i>. (I just finished Neon Genesis Evangelion, would recommend.)<br /> <br /> But the rest of us are discussing &quot;indistinguishable replicants&quot;. I get that this isn't interesting to you, but one <i>can</i> make people out of the Wyld, and the Wyld <i>does</i> warp the personality of those who dwell within it. We're not discussing making an identical clone, we're discussing making a new and unique individual and the issues around identity and the continuity of life. This is the Ship of Theseus crossed with Plato's Cave. I am flabbergasted that you can only see this as adversarial.<br /> <br /> (I also find that your line of reasoning risks raising complex moral questions about the generic humans one may create with Wyld Shaping Technique.)<br /> <br /> To roll this back to Hunter D's Original Post:<br /> <br /> Do you think, then, that a PC should be able to restore things (true and accurate, no jerking around with an exploration of the nature of reality and human consciousness) from the Wyld or not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T13:17:20-08:00","id":1434283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434211#post1434211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this attitude to be very contrary to the usual standards of Exalted regarding player and character agency. A narrative that ends on &quot;you'll never know if this is really who or what you intended to pull out&quot; does not seem well suited.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because the Wyld is one of the places where the setting dips into horror, and specifically existentially unsettling matters. The game itself is pretty clear that being <i>good at things</i> doesn't make you <i>good at being right</i>, and a lot of the problems the Exalted face stem from how Exalted hypercompetence does not extend to being hypercompetent at making judgment calls. And Wyld material that Jenna has influenced, which is a lot of it, deals directly with questions like where do you draw the line between discovery and creation when it comes to discerning meaning?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434211#post1434211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't know, there's the Occult Ability and Charm enhanced insight into people's personalities, I think there are reasonable tools to figure this stuff out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can totally use Occult Charms to figure out that the person you dredged out of the Wyld is at least partially made of Wyld-stuff, and you can definitely use Lore fact declaration Charms to declare this just means they absorbed Wyld-stuff while they were in there. But Wyld-shaping Technique is a Lore Charm. If you're not going &quot;This seems uncomfortably similar to the way Wyld Shaping <i>is itself</i> using essence-charged mastery of lore to declare a truth out of the Wyld,&quot; then, uh... maybe you don't want to engage with those themes? Sure, that's fine.<br /> <br /> But then I've always seen Exalted as being as critical of agency as it is supportive. The horns of that dillemma are <i>why I like the game.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T13:25:28-08:00","id":1434286,"title":"","content":"Also I am kind of of the opinion that when you have the supernatural power to declare truth, that actually should create unsettling questions about truths you think you're discovering and not declaring. Especially when your truth-declaring powers work best in the chaos beyond the world and you're trying to discover lost truths out in the chaos beyond the world. Like, dude. That seems like an <i>inevitable</i> tradeoff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T16:51:29-08:00","id":1434307,"title":"","content":"...I was about to say something about how introducing a fact is a purely out-of-character action but Prophet of Seventeen Cycles and God-King\u2019s Shrike suddenly pulled up and asked me how I\u2019m doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T22:41:24-08:00","id":1434347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434307#post1434307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I was about to say something about how introducing a fact is a purely out-of-character action but Prophet of Seventeen Cycles and God-King\u2019s Shrike suddenly pulled up and asked me how I\u2019m doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Lore Charm thing, and it's really nifty, but it doesn't help unravel the ontological problems the Wyld presents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T00:25:43-08:00","id":1434353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434307#post1434307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I was about to say something about how introducing a fact is a purely out-of-character action but Prophet of Seventeen Cycles and God-King\u2019s Shrike suddenly pulled up and asked me how I\u2019m doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dogstar Ruminations is particularly apt.<br /> <br /> &quot;My great knowledge has <i>observed</i> this thing which will happen. Totally didn't cause it. <i>Totally</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T02:38:27-08:00","id":1434361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434154#post1434154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If whatever you pull out of the Wyld is a bit off, does that mean they're fake, or are they just exhibiting the natural effects of having had experiences in the Wyld? If you're looking for a fantastic, legendary magical vase sculpted by a famous First Age sculptor that was lost in such-and-such Wyld incursion, and what you get out of the Wyld is a bit warped, is that because you made it wrong or was it warped by spending centuries in the Wyld? If you're too committed to finding the one that <i>isn't</i> warped, are you likely to reject the &quot;real thing&quot; and settle for something you create out of your conceptions instead? Or is refusing to settle for a warped copy and commitment to finding the original... an act of will on your part that can repair the vase to its original state, assuming that being lost to the Wyld means it becomes of the Wyld and becomes subject to the process of Wyld shaping?</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, though, we have the makings of an objectivity test baked into our premise, ala &quot;recovering&quot;. Essentially a variant of a teleporter problem.<br /> <br /> Two Solars, working independently on opposite sides of Creation with no knowledge of each other a week apart, both try to recover the same unique, legendary vase.<br /> <br /> If the process recovers &quot;the&quot; vase, then the second Solar will get a 404 - file not found. The second Solar won't necessarily know why her efforts failed, but the Hypothetical Omniscient Perceiver does - objectively, the vase has already been recovered, so it has been made *unrecoverable* by definition.<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, both Solars get vases, then at least one got a &quot;fake&quot;, and lacking any reason to prefer one reference frame over the other, we have to conclude that they're *both* fakes, or at least that the definition of &quot;fake&quot; must be subjective (and/or meaningless).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-03-2021, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T05:26:49-08:00","id":1434372,"title":"","content":"Couldn't we just get two copies of the vase? Like the Lasting Damage I and II.<br /> <br /> Kirk steps into the transporter and arrives in two different places - why can't both Kirk's be &quot;real&quot;? Maybe a good version and an evil version in true transporter paradox fashion, but why not two identical duplicates - exactly the same in every way?<br /> <br /> (I mean, that's kinda the point of Thomas Riker.)<br /> <br /> Two Solars, working independently on opposite sides of Creation try to recover a vase. The Solar PC in your game who doesn't know about the other Solar recovers a vase. The Hypothetical Omniscient Perceiver (i.e. the ST) might know if the other Solar 404'd, or got a vase, or if both the vases are fake, or if both the vases are real, but the Solar PC who recovered that vase does not have that information.<br /> <br /> And given the flow of time in the Wyld, isn't it possible that a vase might be lost, recovered, lost again, then recovered again? And not, neccessarily, in that order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T12:34:56-08:00","id":1434410,"title":"","content":"I mean, things that are Lost to The Wyld aren't obliterated. This isn't the Maw of Oblivion. They are changed over and over again until they no longer resemble the mundane matter they once were, but there's a chain of causation between what they were and what they are now. It's just impossibly long and convoluted and bizarre.<br /> <br /> I would think the main thing about recovering something lost to the Wyld would be finding what it has Become. Be it a hobgoblin, or a part of the shine in a Behemoth's eternal mane, or a combination of 138 places/objects/feelings.<br /> <br /> You can use WST to remake the vase but to say it was the same vase would require you to find its component parts, the relevant charms would be Investigation. Likely branching off Evidence-Discerning Method or its upgrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T17:46:20-08:00","id":1434440,"title":"","content":"Personally I deliberately refrained from answering \u201cYou\u2019re looking for Order-Affirming Blow\u201d to see where the thread would go if I didn\u2019t but I guess we\u2019ve finally arrived there regardless. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T18:41:27-08:00","id":1434444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434440#post1434440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I deliberately refrained from answering \u201cYou\u2019re looking for Order-Affirming Blow\u201d to see where the thread would go if I didn\u2019t but I guess we\u2019ve finally arrived there regardless. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait no I take it back.<br /> Undo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T23:37:29-08:00","id":1434460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1434440#post1434440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I deliberately refrained from answering \u201cYou\u2019re looking for Order-Affirming Blow\u201d to see where the thread would go if I didn\u2019t but I guess we\u2019ve finally arrived there regardless. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends how lost the thing is. But, sure, why not?<br /> <br /> Mortals slap people to their senses. Solars punch the Wyld off.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I don't like the idea of causal do-overs in Creation. But the point of the Wyld is that it's a roiling, alien, sea of possibilities and myth where the rigid laws of Creation break down.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with punching a scarecrow to turn him back into the missing prince from the neighbouring kingdom <i>in the Wyld</i>.<br /> <br /> If your Lore Supernal or Essence 3 Solar starts in Creation, I still think you should need to go on some sort of epic quest to <i>find</i> the scarecrow/prince first. (Possibly invovling Evidence-Discerning Method and the like to track down the missing prince, or the pieces of the missing prince Isis-style. Possibly an unrelated love story about an interdimensional wizard who eats hearts and the lost prince is only incidental.) I don't think &quot;I spend 15m touching this random piece of wood I thought was a walking stick and magically recover the lost prince&quot; is a satisfying story. But <i>ending</i> the quest with Order Affirming Blow is on-point.<br /> <br /> Solars should be able to recover things lost to the Wyld.<br /> <br /> (Non-Solars might need a Working, or a rare artifact, or the aid of a powerful patron, or other, specialised, magics instead of one Lore Charm with no prerequisites. But they should still be able to recover things.)<br /> <br /> (And I don't think you can touch a &quot;Lost Kingdom&quot; and restore the whole thing with Order Affirming Blow. But the fact that OAB requires that you have the Wyld twisted thing in order to touch it is enough of a restriction for me -- as the Wyld is basically infinite.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-04-2021, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T10:17:31-08:00","id":1434497,"title":"","content":"For the Order-Affirming blow to work, it's still required for the person/object to be restored to be whole (even if changed). Moreover, the charm doesn't state what happens if it gets used on objects that are created from wyld <i>in imitation</i> of something creation-based. So, again, we get back to two things:<br /> <br /> First, the thing we want restored may be one that was lost in Wyld, but cannot be really lost <i>to</i> Wyld. The parts of Creation (be it land, objects or people) that were dissolved into the Wyld during Balorian crusade might be recreated, but they cannot be restored. They are truly gone.<br /> <br /> Second, considering the nature of the Wyld, it may still be really hard to differentiate between finding a thing that was lost there, and having the wyld <i>create</i> for you the thing you look for.<br /> Stuff like two different Solars looking for a certain unique object within the Wyld, and both obtaining one (with both being certain that their find is the real one), should still be something that can happen.<br /> <br /> There may be some special cases where getting a duplicate should be far less possible, (like looking for an object/person/location that is protected from Wyld in some way) and some methods to minimize the possibility of our desire to find something influencing our results (i.e. by not having the search and identification process being done by the same person), but the certainty should almost never reach 100%.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T10:21:40-08:00","id":1434498,"title":"","content":"Also Order-Affirming Blow forces a Raksha into a form based on their Intimacies to a Solar. Which could be... interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T13:50:30-08:00","id":1434524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433982-recoving-things-lost-to-the-wyld?p=1433991#post1433991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so if I wanted to recover SOULS but not the persons attached to them what would that entail?<br /> <br /> I Will bring the Dragon Kings and other dead races back and You WILL NOT stop me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have been quite curious about this goal, myself.<br /> <br /> Every time I thought of the Dragon-Kings lost in the Wyld, I've wanted to know if their was a way to salvage their immortal souls &amp; bring them back into Creation.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm also highly interested in reconstituting souls lost to Oblivion. Such is my ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}